// QCC Executor gRPC service.
//
// Mediates between the qcc-controller (Go reconciler) and quantum backends.
// Internally selects a vendor Adapter (Aer for local, IBM via
// qiskit-ibm-runtime, …) and runs transpile → submit → poll →
// fetch_result.  Vendor reach comes from the Qiskit provider ecosystem
// (qiskit.providers.Backend implementations); alternative substrates
// (QRMI for Pasqal/multi-vendor, CUDA-Q for NVIDIA) are Ch9 future-work
// — see QCC-Design-State.md §7d (QEI direction).
//
// Two API shapes coexist:
//
//   * RunCircuit — synchronous, single-RPC end-to-end. Suits in-process
//     simulators (Aer) and short hardware jobs where the controller is happy
//     to block within one reconcile.
//
//   * SubmitTask + WatchTask + FetchTaskResult — async lifecycle aligned
//     with Qiskit's JobV1 contract.  Real-hardware jobs use this path
//     because they queue for minutes; the controller polls via WatchTask
//     and fetches counts via FetchTaskResult on subsequent reconcile passes
//     rather than blocking inside a single RPC.
//
// See docs/systems-design/QCC-System-Design.md §6 (architecture), §9
// (selection model).

